WEBVTT

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.980
What's happening?

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.570
However you look at it...

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.230
...this is Koshien stadium, isn't it?

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:22.910
Hey, weren't we heading to the prefectural ballpark?

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.910
It's true we were aiming for the Koshien, though...

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.690
So we warped right past winning the regional tournament?

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.140
Go us, man.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.500
This is no time for jokes.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.950
This ain't normal.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.120
Yeah, it's weird. Way too quiet.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:44.700
I can't hear any cars, or the sounds of the town...

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.390
We should be able to hear those things.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.430
The Koshien's built in the middle of the desert, isn't it?

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:55.690
<i>Don't go telling me this is the work of aliens again...</i>

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.900
Currently, hundreds of different alien species come and go from the Earth, living their lives.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.100
Species that come in peace...

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.920
Aggressive, warlike species...

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.690
Aliens with all kinds of different personalities live among us,

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:10.350
maintaining a precarious balance.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:12.910
Considering all this,

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:17.320
is it really so shocking that we might stumble into a mystery zone one day?!

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:29.420
The towns entrance is adorned with a cow's skull

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:33.770
It's fine that the law is decided by the strongest,

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.340
But this simple feeling will not be enough to fulfill you

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:44.990
Everyone will definitely revolt and shortly disappear

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:50.110
That's a shocking bloody picture

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:55.450
I'm feeling nauseous

00:01:55.450 --> 00:02:05.830
Holding my head, I board the subway

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:16.010
Righteous way of living, righteous way of dying

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:26.320
Who on earth knows or what the hell can show me?

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:36.820
Cold finger girl

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.940
Sit Down

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.360
The bus disappeared?

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.150
Yes, it did!

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:02.460
And it took Kisaragi High School's baseball team with it, just like that!

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:05.250
Tsutsui-kun was on it too, wasn't he?

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.750
Are you sure you weren't seeing things?

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.250
Please, don't underestimate the eyes of us Disckonians!

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.460
I can see the stitches on a 160 km/h fastball clear as day!

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.300
Tell me exactly what happened.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.380
I was chasing after the baseball team's bus on my bike.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:23.760
I planned on following them 70 kilometers to the prefectural ballpark and cheering them on.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.030
Doing stuff that's going to blow your cover to an Earthling isn't helping.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:28.040
Then...

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:43.500
This seems similar to an incident at the Fujishiro bypass where an automobile disappeared.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.030
It vanished into the fourth dimension?

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:48.570
It was an accident involving a sudden transfer to an alternate space.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:51.040
In an instant, the automobile's particles were disassembled.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:53.050
But, that's...

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:55.860
It's not an accident that happens often.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:04:00.050
We should consider that the bus was thrown into an alternate dimension for some reason.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.430
An alternate dimension, huh?

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.850
What in the world is going on?

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.570
No point in thinkin' about it!

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:17.860
I'm sure this is one of those "porno gaijin" things!

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:21.900
Captain, it's not "porno gaijin!" It's "poltergeist!"

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.580
Who cares one way or the other?

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.040
Since...

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:32.280
...we've made it to the Koshien, everybody run!

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.840
Fifty laps around the field, let's go!

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.670
Sheesh... Even after being swept up in such an abnormal situation...

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.270
Well, that's the captain for you, seriously.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:44.980
He's the kind of guy who eats faster than he can taste.

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:47.180
That's not true!

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:51.680
The captain always says the lunches I make for him are delicious!

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.210
Yeah, sure, thanks for that.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:58.970
The most abnormal situation is that you're goin' out with the captain, Fujii.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.730
I like him, 'kay?!

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.980
This is some poltergeist, right?

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:05.060
Like in the club room...

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.230
This is on a whole different level.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:13.750
Transporting the entire bus to the Koshien is way beyond normal!

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:19.000
So, I know we're all saying "Koshien", but do you really think this is it?

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.960
Huh? But...

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:26.880
Well, I've only seen the Koshien on television...

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.630
Anyone here actually been there?

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:31.330
I have.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.180
Tanaka?!

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.090
I saw a Giants Hanshin game.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:35.740
What do you think?

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:37.480
Something definitely seems different...

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:41.270
There's something I'd like to check, though.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:46.650
Yeah...

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:50.520
They should be here, but the baseball team's bus hasn't arrived.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:51.990
Did something happen?

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.580
We don't know yet.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:55.850
We'll contact you again.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.640
No clues, huh?

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:03.190
This is the work of the Ellarians!

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:03.590
What?

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:09.290
If Tsutsui-san's team makes it to the Koshien, the high schools in their territory might lose!

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:12.280
That's why they decided to play dirty!

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:13.890
That's got to be it!

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.010
We've got no choice but to crush them...

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.140
Hey, hey... Don't jump to conclusions.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:20.510
You have no proof, right?

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.980
We love Kisaragi High School!

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.370
We love Tsutsui-san!

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:30.370
After seeing just how hard that team practiced...

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:34.520
I don't care who it is, from which planet they're from, or why they did it...

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:36.030
I'll definitely won't forgive them!

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:39.660
P-Please calm down!

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:42.390
What, you gonna try and stop us, huh?!

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:46.460
Sado, do you think this really is because of some extraterrestrial?

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.670
That seems to be true for the disappearance of the Norfolk regiment in 1915,

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:53.750
as well as the famous Bermuda Triangle, however...

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:55.170
But perhaps...

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:56.890
This is strange.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:58.920
I'm sure it was here.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.710
What are you looking for?

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:03.400
I stuck an Okayama Bizen High sticker here.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.400
One from the 68th tournament.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.530
Don't you think it'd be taken off?

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.360
But mine isn't there, either...

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:10.270
What isn't?

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:11.950
You see...

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.890
Hey, you shouldn't deface the ballpark!

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:17.790
I feel bad about it, really!

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.870
But I was really little, I didn't know any better.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:22.610
It's weird though.

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:25.300
Even if they erased it, there should still be some traces.

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:27.310
Maybe you got the wrong seat?

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:29.090
I'm sure it was here!

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:31.770
I made sure to memorize it in case I ever came back!

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:35.470
See? Row 15, seat 41...

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.860
There ain't any numbers!

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:39.300
Huh? Why?

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:42.930
Hey, are you sure you went to the Koshien?

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:43.960
I really did!

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:45.400
I'm not kidding!

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:48.900
I think Tanaka-sempai is telling the truth.

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:50.920
Then, what do you mean?

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:52.930
The thing that's different is this ballpark.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:59.290
Basically, this ballpark isn't exactly like the Koshien.

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:07.010
What the hell are you doing here?

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:10.110
Just felt like harassing you for old time's sake, Yukitaka.

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:10.840
And?

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:14.840
I got on the bus so I could cheer everyone on, too, but...

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:18.610
Even I was surprised that something like this happened.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:22.520
Hey! You better not tell me this was your doing, got it?

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:23.840
Get off your high horse.

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:27.110
I wouldn't use this kind of power just to tease little ol' you.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:28.470
Yeah, I wanna kill you.

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:29.950
Haven't felt this bloodlust for a while!

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:31.510
Who is that, exactly?

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.270
Just a little lost stray kitten!

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.530
Everyone, come quick!

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:37.780
We've got trouble!

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:43.120
Whoa... This is unbelievable.

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:45.960
Isn't this Conan City Ballpark?

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:48.920
W-Wait a second.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:52.590
The locker rooms in ballparks all look the same, right?

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:53.970
No, look at that.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:58.120
That washing machine is definitely the one at the municipal ballpark.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:59.680
Yeah, you're right!

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:04.250
Then, if this is Conan City Ballpark...

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.110
That door should lead to the outside.

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:15.040
Where is this?

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:17.030
I feel like I've seen this place somewhere.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:21.120
Yeah, it's where they hold interviews after the high school baseball games.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.850
I don't get it!

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:25.710
Are we in Conan City Ballpark or the Koshien?

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:28.600
Probably, both.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:29.560
Correct!

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:31.480
What do you mean by that?

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:36.000
The only part of the Koshien that's been
reconstructed is the part you can see on TV.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.970
The rest of it was constructed out of ballparks you know.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:43.980
Earlier it was just a conjecture, but after seeing this there's little doubt.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:47.260
This is the inside of someone's mind.

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:51.980
Think about how you'd feel being treated like livestock, won't you?!

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:54.650
And who, do you think, lets you live an easy life?!

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:57.410
All you can ever think about is work, work, work!

00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:59.070
Won't you ever shut the hell up?

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.090
Why won't you understand a little how hard I work?!

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:03.080
Stop it!

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:11.630
The mysterious disappearance of a man named Robert in England, 1920.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:15.160
The father appeared suddenly again after a few days,

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:17.940
and he said he had been trapped inside his daughter's mind.

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:23.140
The case is explained as his 6 year old daughter trapping him in her subconscious.

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:26.640
So, you're saying it's not the work of the Ellarians?

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:27.810
Yes.

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:31.650
This extraordinary ability is more often triggered by extreme stress.

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:35.150
The regional qualifying tournament for the Koshien...

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:36.090
Yes.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.780
I can only imagine the stress of the players.

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:43.950
Inside someone's subconscious?

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:46.410
It's the same as that case in England.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:49.880
A paranormal space created by extreme stress.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:51.130
Simply put:

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:53.670
We are trapped inside a dream.

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:42.350
Stop it!

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:00.330
Forgive me!

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:10.330
So when the father repented, the girl's stress was relieved,

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:13.450
and he was returned from within her subconscious?

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:14.910
Exactly.

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:18.870
To get out of here we should get rid of the source of the stress.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.150
Easy to say, but...

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:22.880
Who is it?

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:25.200
Someone who's scared, right?

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:30.130
I'm sure it's someone who's thinking like "I want to go to the Koshien, but if I lose, then..."

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:34.430
So the person's thinking about going to the Koshien, but not the regional championship?

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.730
This ain't some joke!

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:43.520
Doesn't anyone have a hint or something?

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:46.390
I'm so nervous I think I might die!

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:48.050
This year is my last chance, after all.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:50.240
Then, I guess that goes for me, too.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.030
But you guys are here.

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:54.530
Yeah, wait. We're <i>all</i> here!

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.280
Inside one's subconscious, anything goes!

00:12:58.280 --> 00:13:01.650
One of us here is surely a creation of the mind, a fake!

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:06.170
This is it! Time to point fingers!

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:07.510
It might be you!

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.050
Or perhaps it's you!

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:10.410
No, maybe you.

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:13.010
Suspect everyone except for yourself!

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:17.320
And suspect even yourself of being the fake, for suspecting everyone else!

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:18.810
Shut the hell up!

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:20.840
Stop trying to plant doubt!

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:23.440
You think having us all turn on each other would be fun?

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:25.270
Yeah, totally.

00:13:28.230 --> 00:13:30.600
You bastard!

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:33.240
What's everyone looking so down for?

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:37.060
You guys should be more like Tsutsui and get a workout!

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.090
There might be no point to searching for the culprit.

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:42.210
Why not, Kanemitsu?

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:46.250
Whoever it was ran away from the stress of the regional championships.

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:49.040
If we could finish the final game, we could go home.

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:52.510
But we can't do that while we're in here.

00:13:57.280 --> 00:14:00.280
Looks like we're in an eternal paradox!

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:07.060
W-What?

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.240
No way... But there's no one here.

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:18.050
A cheering section with no people...

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:19.540
Surreal.

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:22.000
W-Whoa, look at that.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:25.750
Isn't that the representative for Ehime, Matsukawa Shogyou?

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:28.270
Their big gun, Imai, is there too.

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:31.760
That's definitely the top seed for this year's tournament, Matsusho.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:36.260
We got beat bad in an exhibition game with them last year, didn't we?

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:39.480
That's it! This is a dream!

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:41.520
Goin' to the Koshien is definitely our dream!

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:44.070
Captain, that's not it...

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:44.520
Okay!

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:49.860
Beat Matsusho to a bloody pulp, and get pumped for our game with Nittoudai Yamagata!

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.920
What, he wants us to play them?

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:54.360
No one can stop him now.

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:58.970
Why not? I wanted to play Matsusho with our team this year.

00:14:58.970 --> 00:14:59.900
Let's do it!

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:04.910
Looks like we're playing the championship game after all.

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:06.330
Well, not the prefectural one, though.

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:10.780
If we can get rid of the stress this way, we should be able to return.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.630
I sure hope so...

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:26.940
What's wrong with everyone?

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.940
Kisaragi High's in trouble with runners on first and second and no outs!

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:30.940
How are they gonna get through this?

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:34.960
Terakado, Satou... They're playin' like they're scared.

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:36.530
Well then, I'm gonna...

00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:39.600
You idiot!

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:40.820
You got runners on base!

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:44.500
The guy with the problem's at the station?

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:45.840
Yes.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:49.300
Edogawa-san said that one of the regulars got to the station alone.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:51.280
It must be him, then.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:55.560
But if the stress is from the qualifying championship, there's nothing we can do about it.

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:59.450
We have to at least move him to a location where Tsutsui-kun and the bus itself

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:02.820
won't get into an accident if they return.

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:05.020
We've got to rescue them quick, or else...

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:07.060
There's only two hours until the game!

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:08.230
But...

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:11.950
The prince would consider every option, no matter how underhanded...

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:14.230
What is it?

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:18.960
Mr. Prince said that he was gonna hide in the luggage compartment and sneak aboard the bus.

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:35.970
Craft-san, what exactly...

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.380
I'm sure he's doing his utmost to think up a plan.

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:41.520
<i>Think, Craft.</i>

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.280
<i>This is a one in a million chance!</i>

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:50.270
<i>There has to be some way to keep him sealed up while returning Tsutsui-kun and the others to reality!</i>

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:52.900
<i>Nope!</i>

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:57.690
Captain, you can never go to the dark side.

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:00.970
Shit!

00:17:00.970 --> 00:17:03.740
That Imai bastard hit a home-run off of me!

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:05.710
Don't worry, they only scored five runs.

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:10.040
But I was always so calm in my image training!

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:10.570
Terakado-senpai is acting suspicious.

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:15.860
He's already made three errors, so I think he's more nervous than anyone.

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.460
I think it's Fujii.

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:21.890
It's always the young girls that cause poltergeists, you know.

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:26.400
It's the captain whose mind isn't on the same track as a normal person's.

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:26.400
Tokorozawa, hit that wimpy pitch right back outta there!

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:29.490
I think it's odd that he hasn't changed a bit since we got here.

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:31.190
You have a good eye.

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:36.410
This illusion is caused by one's subconscious... Their outward nervousness is irrelevant.

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:37.190
Or rather...

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:39.830
It's the ones thinking calmly that are most suspect!

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:43.440
And the calmest people here are you two!

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:44.790
Enough already.

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:48.710
Yes! Straight through the hole!

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:52.420
We're playing Matsusho at the Koshien...

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:54.000
If we don't enjoy ourselves, it's our loss!

00:17:58.360 --> 00:17:59.090
Him?

00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:03.760
Um, you really think it's the stress of the championships that's the cause?

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:04.390
What are you getting at?

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:09.000
I do image training before swimming meets.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:12.640
I clear everything from my mind except for the times I swam well...

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:17.400
The more I concentrate, the faster time seems to pass.

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:21.900
I see. It's not stress that has piled up to extremes, it's concentration!

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:23.690
What do you mean?

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:27.580
It's the same principle of working your mind to its maximum.

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:31.410
In fact, concentration would be even more likely to trigger an extraordinary ability!

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:33.910
So then, while he was on the bus...

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:37.420
He was doing image training for the championship game.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:40.420
Then, the club members were all suddenly sucked inside!

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:44.400
In that case, why hasn't everyone returned?

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:48.890
Shouldn't he just have to concentrate the same amount as when he made the bus disappear?

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:50.680
There is a high possibility of that.

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:53.980
But he doesn't have time to be concentrating on baseball right now.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:58.540
No, I think it's rather that he can think of nothing else.

00:18:58.540 --> 00:18:59.610
Why is that?

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:03.330
The Kisaragi 9 are there in his subconscious.

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:07.700
If we seriously consider the effects of such outside stimuli...

00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:13.470
All right! No outs, and runners on first and second!

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:17.390
Batting second, Third Base, Kanemitsu-kun!

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:18.330
Play ball!

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:20.950
If we don't enjoy ourselves, it's our loss, huh?

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:23.730
Maybe you're right, Yukitaka...

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:29.420
That's how it's done, Kanemitsu!

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:31.850
That's why you're the smoothest operator in Kisaragi!

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:32.770
Bases loaded!

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:34.020
We're counting on you, Kuramoto!

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:36.370
Bag o' ice!

00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:38.810
Get yer bag o' ice here, only at the Koshien!

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:42.850
Batting fourth, Right Field, Iwata-kun.

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:52.540
I'm callin' it now! A grand slam!

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.630
Go for it, captain!

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.260
A kiss is waitin' for ya if you hit it!

00:19:57.260 --> 00:19:59.000
OK, baby.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:07.760
Yeah!

00:20:08.650 --> 00:20:11.280
Woohoo! It's a grand slam!

00:20:12.860 --> 00:20:13.790
We're even!

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:15.770
Finally, all square!

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:18.650
All right! Now's the time for a comeback!

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:23.540
It ain't stress, is it?

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:24.510
Nope.

00:20:24.510 --> 00:20:28.320
The only thing in their heads is going to the Koshien.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:29.540
This sucks.

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:33.610
If stress wasn't the cause, then the plans I thought up are worthless.

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:35.750
Just for reference, let's hear 'em.

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:37.160
Plan number one:

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:40.700
Use a psychological test to identify the culprit and force them to quit the team.

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:44.710
By applying such heavy pressure we'll be released and return to reality.

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:46.700
Plan number two:

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:49.790
Destroy the Koshien, which the culprit regards as holy ground.

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:54.390
If we do that, then their defensive mechanism will kick us out of this world itself.

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:55.920
Plan number three:

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:59.780
Do such wicked things at this place that even the culprit himself won't be able to stand it.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:00.380
If we do that, then he will...

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:04.150
You evil bastard!

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:20.150
We're gonna win, and we're gonna go to the Koshien!

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:24.990
If we don't win here, we can't finish things with Matsukawasho, you know?

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:25.790
Huh? What?

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:28.030
The captain must've been dreaming again!

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:28.800
Yup.

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:31.620
Okay, let's do it!

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:37.140
Oh? Not going to watch the game?

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:41.550
I'd feel bad if Tsutsui-kun's luck ran out thanks to me being around.

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:43.890
He's actually quite wary of jinxing things.

00:21:45.270 --> 00:21:48.860
The players are all really revved up since they've returned.

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:53.660
They must've had a nice match in the dream world.

00:21:54.440 --> 00:21:56.930
But, aren't we forgetting something?

00:21:56.930 --> 00:21:59.830
Something I feel like I don't want to remember...

00:22:00.470 --> 00:22:02.250
<i>Tonight's gonna be a celebration!</i>

00:22:15.530 --> 00:22:16.890
So...

00:22:18.070 --> 00:22:20.480
How should I get back?

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:27.230
Are you ready?

00:22:27.520 --> 00:22:38.030
Do not fear 'The Now' searching for something that can't be seen across this infinite distance

00:22:38.030 --> 00:22:52.250
Under the hundred million glittering lights, I found you searching for your dream

00:22:52.250 --> 00:23:01.010
An infinite world filled with glass shards

00:23:02.180 --> 00:23:13.070
Growing up I felt I knew many meaningless things

00:23:13.070 --> 00:23:20.530
Shining like a jewel, you soar in the sky, no past, no future

00:23:20.530 --> 00:23:25.870
The answer is beyond the sky

00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:36.380
Do not fear 'The Dream', in a distant
place where truth and lies are unseen

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:52.110
Under the hundred million glittering lights, flowers sway in the wind

00:23:56.680 --> 00:23:58.370
I'm being chased! Hide me!

00:23:58.370 --> 00:23:59.100
By who?

00:23:59.100 --> 00:24:00.470
My betrothed, and my little brother...

00:24:00.470 --> 00:24:03.020
How did such a crazy bill pass the legislature?!

00:24:03.020 --> 00:24:05.190
How do you do, my beloved prince?

00:24:05.190 --> 00:24:07.300
This is beautiful!

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:08.240
Why can't you understand?

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:10.590
I'll wait here, so can you buy me something?

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:13.750
Why don't you go back to your home planet and become the king or something?

00:24:13.750 --> 00:24:16.110
Now, big bro, put on the ring!

00:24:16.110 --> 00:24:18.210
Next time: Half moon...!

00:24:18.210 --> 00:24:21.400
Things are gonna get busy...
